From bc0d11cb76e823349d95685db2567bf4f598a53a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chuppatricky <74110004+chuppatricky@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:24:49 -0600
Subject: fix(libc): answer /app0 lookups under Wine from one listing per
 directory

Wine matches each path component case-insensitively itself: on a
case-sensitive Linux file system a lookup of a missing name lists its
whole directory, once for every Win32 call made on that path, and Wine
does not implement FileCaseSensitiveInfo, so MatchNames listed it once
more (with a stat per entry). Astro Bot looks up thousands of missing
names in data/prein/*/odx (2,500-24,500 entries) while a level loads:
~25 ms each, 2-6 minutes per level and multi-second stalls on the main
thread (the galaxy flight drops to ~3 fps). Most of those lookups are
module lookups: sceKernelStat, lstat and read-only sceKernelOpen resolve
with module=true (a missing last name may be a relinked
<name>.guest.prx), which make six Win32 calls per missing name.

Under Wine:
- every directory counts as case-insensitive, so a name is matched
  with one FindFirstFileExW instead of a full listing;
- /app0 (read-only game content) names are answered from one listing
  per directory (ReadOnlyNameCache), module lookups included: a name
  found resolves to its on-disk spelling, which Wine finds without
  listing; a missing name resolves into the empty
  Build/RunHybrid/_aps5_absent, so every caller still reports ENOENT
  from its own calls, and Wine answers them at once.
Names the cache does not match exactly as the resolver does (non-ASCII,
wildcards, '.', '..', a trailing separator, two entries differing only
in case, a file used as a directory, a missing last name of a module
lookup with a relinked module beside it) resolve the usual way. Off on
Windows, with app0.zar, and with APS5_NO_APP0_NAME_CACHE.
